# Deception

Deception is framed as a universal mental model—a conceptual tool for navigating complex situations through pattern recognition. It is cross-referenced to Dan Ariely's *The Honest Truth About Dishonesty*, which provides empirical grounding through experiments on dishonesty, self-deception, and rationalization.

## Key Source

- [[The Honest Truth About Dishonesty - Dan Ariely]]

## Summary

The model applies across domains and connects to existing concepts like [[cognitive-biases-library]], [[confirmation-bias]], [[illusion-of-control]], and [[morality-and-decision-making]].
